      "urpx:forRatePlan": {
        "@id": "ladwp:r-1a"
      },
      "urpx:hasCoverageClaim": {
        "@id": "ladwp:cc-r-1a-2026-07-01",
        "@type": "urpx:CoverageClaim",
        "urpx:completenessResult": {
          "@id": "urpx:partial"
        },
        "urpx:selfContained": true,
        "urpx:explainedBy": {
          "@type": "urpx:Evaluation",
          "@id": "ladwp:cc-r-1a-2026-07-01-evaluation",
          "urpx:evaluationKind": {
            "@id": "urpx:coverageEvaluation"
          },
          "urpx:description": "This filing does not carry everything its source document states. 2 parts are deferred, listed here in the same words as the filing's tariff.toml [modeling].deferrals so the two records cannot drift. (1) Zone 1 / Zone 2 selector absent. Page 1 of the source PDF prices two tier ladders at identical per-tier rates but different breakpoints (Zone 1: first 350 / next 700 / above 1050 kWh; Zone 2: first 500 / next 1000 / above 1500 kWh). The model folds zone into serviceTierNumber (tiers 1-3 Zone 1, tiers 4-6 Zone 2) inside one ServiceTiers container over one kWh MetricInput, so the brackets overlap and only the tier urpx:name strings say which ladder to walk. URPX v0.5.1 expresses this directly: PlanElements.hasProfileAlternatives with an AlternativeDimension.customDimensionProperty of 'serviceZone', plus ServiceBracket.referencesProfileAlternative on each bracket. The corpus already ships that shape for a geographic dimension in us/ca/pge/electricity/e-1/versions/2026-03-01/rate-plan_pge_e-1_2026-03-01.jsonld (baseline territory P through Z). This is work, not a blocker: the target shape is 3 tiers carrying 2 zone-keyed brackets each, in place of the 6 flattened tiers this filing carries. (2) Minimum Charge composition not modeled. Page 1 prices a $10.00 per month Minimum Charge and footnotes it '(1) Plus ECA, ESA and RCA', so the floor is $10.00 plus the three capped-ordinance per-kWh adjustments on actual usage. The $10.00 is carried as ladwp:r-1a-2026-07-01-price-minimum-charge with chargeType urpx:minimumBill and intervalDuration P1M; the 'plus ECA, ESA and RCA' composition is not carried anywhere. Separately, no URPX construct enforces a 'greater of' floor, which is a standard-level gap recorded corpus-wide rather than per filing.",
          "urpx:evaluatedOn": "2026-10-07T00:00:00"
        }
      }
    }
  }
